k?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186138699 1071 "In a lottery draw, $308$ people won a consolation prize of $$75$. By rounding both numbers to the nearest ten, estimate how many dollars the lottery paid in consolation prizes in total." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186138699 1071 "In a lottery draw, $308$ people won a consolation prize of $\\$75$. By rounding both numbers to the nearest ten, estimate how many dollars the lottery paid in consolation prizes in total." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186138739 1071 "The price of an insurance policy $p$, in dollars, varies directly with the **square** of the number of incidents $i$ reported by the subscriber in the previous year. If $p = $800$ when the subscriber reported $2$ incidents, then what is the constant of variation? You do not need to state the units.The constant of variation is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186138739 1071 "The price of an insurance policy $p$, in dollars, varies directly with the **square** of the number of incidents $i$ reported by the subscriber in the previous year. If $p = \\$800$ when the subscriber reported $2$ incidents, then what is the constant of variation? You do not need to state the units.The constant of variation is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186138782 1071 "Richard wants to buy a pair of shoes. The store has a special promotion: if the customer posts a photo of the shoes on social media, the price for that customer will decrease for each \"like\" that the photo gets. The store charges $$33.25$ for one like, $$32.50$ for two likes, $$31.75$ for three likes, and so on. If this trend continues, how many likes did Richard get if he paid $$27.25$ for the shoes?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 131941395394