swers to find the value of $36\\times 19$." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186142552 1071 "Ann wishes to find the value of $36\\times 19$. She starts by writing both factors in expanded form.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle 36 = {\\color{blue}{30}}+{\\color{blue}{6}},\\qquad 19 = {\\color{red}{10}}+{\\color{red}{9}}\n$$\n\nThen, she proceeds as follows:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle 30 \\cdot 10|= \\phantom{000}; 30 \\cdot 9|= \\phantom{000}; 6 \\cdot 10|= \\phantom{10}; 6 \\cdot 9|= \\phantom{10}\n$$\n\nFind the missing numbers, and use your answers to find the value of $36\\times 19$." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186142552 1074 "We can compute $36\\times 19$ by filling in the missing numbers and adding the results. So, let's find the missing values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n30 \\cdot 10 &= [math]\\,300\\,[/math] \\\\\n30 \\cdot 9 &= [math]\\,270\\,[/math] \\\\\n6 \\cdot 10 &= [math]\\,60\\,[/math] \\\\\n6 \\cdot 9 &= [math]\\,54\\,[/math]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now add these results:\n\n$$\n1; 3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ + & 2\\end{vmatrix}7\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\\\ +\\end{vmatrix}6\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\\\ +\\end{vmatrix}5\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{vmatrix}8 \\mid 4\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n36\\times 19 = 684\n$$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186142552 1074 "We can compute $36\\times 19$ by filling in the missing numbers and adding the results. So, let's find the missing values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n30 \\cdot 10 &= \\,300\\, \\\\\n30 \\cdot 9 &= \\,270\\, \\\\\n6 \\cdot 10 &= \\,60\\, \\\\\n6 \\cdot 9 &= \\,54\\,\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now add these results:\n\n$$\n1; 3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ + & 2\\end{vmatrix}7\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\\\ +\\end{vmatrix}6\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\\\ +\\end{vmatrix}5\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{vmatrix}8 \\mid 4\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n36\\times 19 = 684\n$$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186142712 1074 "First, recall that the volume of a rectangular package can be calculated as\n\n$$\nV = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nand we are told that this volume is equal to $75 \\, \\text{in}^3$.\n\n![](images/32/32798500f85c9bc6dfc97b588d787ec9befd8a4f5b52aa0bc482588f71ca989f.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n$75 = \\boxed{ {\\hspace{0.167em} \\phantom{0} \\hspace{0.167em}}}\\times 6 \\times 2.5$\n\nSo, since\n\n$$\n6 \\times 2.5 = 15\n$$\n\n, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n75 &= [math]\\,\\phantom{0}\\,[/math] \\cdot \\underbrace{6 \\cdot 2.5}_{15} \\\\\n75 &= [math]\\,\\phantom{0}\\,[/math] \\cdot 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the relationship between multiplication and division, we obtain that the length of the package must be\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\boxed{ {\\hspace{0.167em} \\phantom{0} \\hspace{0.167em}}} = 75 \\div 15 = 5 \\, \\text{in}.\n$$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186142712 1074 "First, recall that the volume of a rectangular package can be calculated as\n\n$$\nV = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nand we are told that this volume is equal to $75 \\, \\text{in}^3$.\n\n![](images/32/32798500f85c9bc6dfc97b588d787ec9befd8a4f5b52aa0bc482588f71ca989f.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n$75 = \\boxed{ {\\hspace{0.167em} \\phantom{0} \\hspace{0.167em}}}\\times 6 \\times 2.5$\n\nSo, since\n\n$$\n6 \\times 2.5 = 15\n$$\n\n, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n75 &= \\,\\phantom{0}\\, \\cdot \\underbrace{6 \\cdot 2.5}_{15} \\\\\n75 &= \\,\\phantom{0}\\, \\cdot 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the relationship between multiplication and division, we obtain that the length of the package must be\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\boxed{ {\\hspace{0.167em} \\phantom{0} \\hspace{0.167em}}} = 75 \\div 15 = 5 \\, \\text{in}.\n$$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186142716 1071 "In a bank account, deposits are presented by positive numbers and withdrawals by negative numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- A transaction of $-\\$4$ means that $\\$4$ were withdrawn.\n- If the balance changes from $-\\$3$ to $\\$2$, it increases by $\\$5$.\n- A balance cannot be less than $\\$0$." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186142716 1071 "In a bank account, deposits are presented by positive numbers and withdrawals by negative numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- A transaction of $-\\[math]4$ means that $\\[/math]4$ were withdrawn.\n- If the balance changes from $-\\[math]3$ to $\\[/math]2$, it increases by $\\[math]5$.\n- A balance cannot be less than $\\[/math]0$." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186142716 1074 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- A negative transaction means the number is on the left side of zero on the number line. The number $-4$ is $4$ units to the left of zero, which represents removing $4$ dollars from the account.![](images/aa/aaa17c446b687ba522a8cf12c6cd14d62fb71f80a4d5c3b23debf5144f595917.png)\nTherefore, this statement is *True.*\n\n- To find the increase, we count how many units the balance moves upward on the number line. From $-3$ to $0$ is an increase of $3$ dollars. From $0$ to $2$ is another increase of $2$ dollars.![](images/bf/bf02b81be6acc08de7d4aee41e97c8a73bba7364a49f6df434c9d7850c3da1e3.png)\nSo, the total increase is $3 + 2 = 5$ dollars.Therefore, this statement is *True.*\n- The number $0$ is on the number line exactly between positive and negative numbers. It represents a balance that is not below zero and not above zero. Since there could be negative balances, a balance could be less than $\\$0$.![](images/ce/ce3df042347c3d502d9b631e1c8978eaf1c5fd2348c1d8d1352af19058082a5e.png)Therefore, this statement is *False.*" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186142716 1074 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- A negative transaction means the number is on the left side of zero on the number line. The number $-4$ is $4$ units to the left of zero, which represents removing $4$ dollars from the account.![](images/aa/aaa17c446b687ba522a8cf12c6cd14d62fb71f80a4d5c3b23debf5144f595917.png)\nTherefore, this statement is *True.*\n\n- To find the increase, we count how many units the balance moves upward on the number line. From $-3$ to $0$ is an increase of $3$ dollars. From $0$ to $2$ is another increase of $2$ dollars.![](images/bf/bf02b81be6acc08de7d4aee41e97c8a73bba7364a49f6df434c9d7850c3da1e3.png)\nSo, the total increase is $3 + 2 = 5$ dollars.Therefore, this statement is *True.*\n- The number $0$ is on the number line exactly between positive and negative numbers. It represents a balance that is not below zero and not above zero. Since there could be negative balances, a balance could be less than $\\[math]0$.![](images/ce/ce3df042347c3d502d9b631e1c8978eaf1c5fd2348c1d8d1352af19058082a5e.png)Therefore, this statement is *False.*" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186143135 1071 "Each copy of a recently published book on mathematics costs $$28$. How much would the school library have to pay to purchase $8$ copies of the book?" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186143135 1071 "Each copy of a recently published book on mathematics costs $\\$28$. How much would the school library have to pay to purchase $8$ copies of the book?" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186143209 1071 "Insert the missing numbers in the pattern below, given that the rule for this pattern is \"subtract $9$.\"$39$,\n{{field-1}} $, 21$,\n{{field-2}}\n$$,\n{{field-3}}" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186143209 1071 "Insert the missing numbers in the pattern below, given that the rule for this pattern is \"subtract $9$.\"$39$,\n{{field-1}} $, 21$,\n{{field-2}}\n,\n{{field-3}}" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186143210 1071 "Insert the missing numbers in the pattern below, given that the rule for this pattern is \"multiply by $2$.\"$1$,\n{{field-1}} $$,\n{{field-2}}\n$, 8$,\n{{field-3}}\n$, 32$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186143210 1071 "Insert the missing numbers in the 