$ is the value of the initial deposit. If there is $\\$8100$ in the account $4$ years after the initial deposit was made, how much money was initially deposited?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147763 1071 "During a charity fundraiser, the mean donation made by each of the $85$ attendees was $$46$. What was the total amount of money raised at the event?The total amount of money raised at the event is $$$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186147763 1071 "During a charity fundraiser, the mean donation made by each of the $85$ attendees was $\\$46$. What was the total amount of money raised at the event?The total amount of money raised at the event is \\$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147767 1074 "The number of views $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $250%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=90$ is the total number of views initially\n\n- $r=2.5$ is the growth rate ($250%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours) after upload\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=90\\cdot (1+2.5)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=90\\cdot (3.5)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of views after $3$ hours, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=90\\cdot (3.5)^{3}≈3859\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of views after $3$ hours is $3859.$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186147767 1074 "The number of views $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $250\\%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=90$ is the total number of views initially\n\n- $r=2.5$ is the growth rate ($250\\%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours) after upload\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=90\\cdot (1+2.5)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=90\\cdot (3.5)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of views after $3$ hours, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=90\\cdot (3.5)^{3}≈3859\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of views after $3$ hours is $3859.$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147797 1071 "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$20%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186147797 1071 "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$20\\%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147797 1074 "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $20%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n20%=\\frac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{2÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}<\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{5},$ \nwhich is $\\text{smaller than}$ $\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186147797 1074 "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $20\\%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n20\\%=\\frac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{2÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}<\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20\\%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{5},$ \nwhich is $\\text{smaller than}$ $\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147799 1071 "Matt and Abraham have the same number of marbles. A total of $63%$ of Matt's marbles are blue, while $\\frac{3}{4}$ of Abraham's marbles are blue. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\n$\\,$\nA total of \n{{field-1}}\nof Abraham's marbles are blue. \n\n$\\,$\nTherefore, he has \n{{field-2}}\nblue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186147799 1071 "Matt and Abraham have the same number of marbles. A total of $63\\%$ of Matt's marbles are blue, while $\\frac{3}{4}$ of Abraham's marbles are blue. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\n$\\,$\nA total of \n{{field-1}}\nof Abraham's marbles are blue. \n\n$\\,$\nTherefore, he has \n{{field-2}}\nblue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147799 1074 "We need to compare $\\frac{3}{4}$ with $63%.$ We can do this by writing $\\frac{3}{4}$ as a percent.\n\nFirst, we write $\\frac{3}{4}$ as an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{75}{100}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{75}{100}=75%\n$$\n\nSince $75%>63%,$ we have the following:\n\n- A total of $75%$ of Abraham's marbles are blue.\n\n- Therefore, he has $\\text{more}$ blue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139539458 17592186576411 false] [17592186147799 1074 "We need to compare $\\frac{3}{4}$ with $63\\%.$ We can do this by writing $\\frac{3}{4}$ as a percent.\n\nFirst, we write $\\frac{3}{4}$ as an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{75}{100}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{75}{100}=75\\%\n$$\n\nSince $75\\%>63\\%,$ we have the following:\n\n- A total of $75\\%$ of Abraham's marbles are blue.\n\n- Therefore, he has $\\text{more}$ blue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139539458 17592186576411 true] [17592186147801 1071 "Lionel and David are youth soccer players. In the previous seas